🐳 Docker Complete Lab Command Sheet
1. Docker Check / Version
docker --version
docker version
docker info
Check Docker service:

sudo systemctl status docker
Start Docker:

sudo systemctl start docker
Enable Docker at boot:

sudo systemctl enable docker
Restart Docker:

sudo systemctl restart docker

2. Docker Images
Download image from Docker Hub
docker pull nginx

Specific version:

docker pull nginx:latest

docker pull nginx:1.25

List images:

docker images

or:

docker image ls

Remove image:

docker rmi nginx

Force remove:

docker rmi -f nginx

Remove unused images:

docker image prune

Remove all unused images:

docker image prune -a

3. Docker Containers
Create and run container
docker run nginx

Usually you want background mode:

docker run -d nginx

Give container a name:

docker run -d --name mynginx nginx

Run with port:

docker run -d --name mynginx -p 8080:80 nginx

Meaning:

-p HOST_PORT:CONTAINER_PORT

8080:80
Browser:

http://SERVER-IP:8080
4. List Containers
Running containers:

docker ps

All containers:

docker ps -a

Only container IDs:

docker ps -q

5. Start / Stop / Restart
Start:

docker start mynginx

Stop:

docker stop mynginx

Restart:

docker restart mynginx

Pause:

docker pause mynginx

Unpause:

docker unpause mynginx

6. Remove Containers
Remove stopped container:

docker rm mynginx

Force remove running container:

docker rm -f mynginx

Remove all stopped containers:

docker container prune

7. Container Logs
Very important for troubleshooting:

docker logs mynginx

Live logs:

docker logs -f mynginx

Last 50 lines:

docker logs --tail 50 mynginx

8. Inspect Container
Complete information:

docker inspect mynginx

Container IP:

docker inspect -f '{{range .NetworkSettings.Networks}}{{.IPAddress}}{{end}}' mynginx

9. Execute Commands Inside Container
Open Bash:

docker exec -it mynginx bash

If Bash doesn't exist:

docker exec -it mynginx sh

Then inside:

ls

pwd

cd /usr/share/nginx/html

Exit:

exit

Run a single command without entering:

docker exec mynginx ls

10. Container Resource Usage
docker stats

Specific container:

docker stats mynginx

11. Docker Run Important Options
Name
docker run --name web nginx

Detached
docker run -d nginx

Port
docker run -d -p 8080:80 nginx

Environment variable
docker run -d -e MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD=1234 mysql

Automatically restart
docker run -d --restart unless-stopped nginx

Interactive terminal
docker run -it ubuntu bash

Remove container automatically after exit
docker run --rm ubuntu

12. Dockerfile
Create file:

nano Dockerfile

Example:

FROM nginx:latest

COPY index.html /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html

EXPOSE 80

Create HTML:

nano index.html

Example:

<h1>Hello Docker</h1>

Build image:

docker build -t myweb .

Check:

docker images

Run:

docker run -d --name mywebcontainer -p 8080:80 myweb

Open:

http://SERVER-IP:8080
13. Custom Dockerfile Name
If file is called df instead of Dockerfile:

docker build -f df -t myapp .

Run:

docker run -d --name myapp-container -p 8080:80 myapp

Remember
-f
means Dockerfile name.

-t
means image tag/name.

.
means current directory is the build context.

14. Important Dockerfile Instructions
FROM

Base image.

WORKDIR

Working directory.

COPY

Copy files from host into image.

ADD

Similar to COPY, with additional archive/URL behavior.

RUN

Execute command while building image.

CMD

Default command when container starts.

ENTRYPOINT

Main executable/entry point.

EXPOSE

Documents the port used by the application.

Example:

FROM python:3.12

WORKDIR /app

COPY requirements.txt .

RUN pip install -r requirements.txt

COPY . .

EXPOSE 5000

CMD ["python", "app.py"]

15. Docker Image vs Container
Remember this for viva:

Dockerfile
    ↓
docker build
    ↓
Docker Image
    ↓
docker run
    ↓
Container
Image = blueprint/template

Container = running instance of image

Example:

docker build -t myapp .

creates image.

Then:

docker run myapp

creates container from that image.

16. Docker Volumes
List volumes:

docker volume ls

Create named volume:

docker volume create myvolume

Inspect:

docker volume inspect myvolume

Use volume:

docker run -d \
  --name mysql \
  -v myvolume:/var/lib/mysql \
  mysql:8.4

Format:

-v VOLUME_NAME:CONTAINER_PATH
Example:

-v myvolume:/var/lib/mysql
Remove volume:

docker volume rm myvolume

Remove unused volumes:

docker volume prune

17. Bind Mount
Host folder:

mkdir website

Run:

docker run -d \
  --name nginx \
  -p 8080:80 \
  -v $(pwd)/website:/usr/share/nginx/html \
  nginx

Meaning:

HOST DIRECTORY
      ↓
$(pwd)/website
      :
      ↓
CONTAINER DIRECTORY
/usr/share/nginx/html
Changes on host appear inside container.

18. Anonymous Volume
docker run -d \
  -v /var/lib/mysql \
  mysql:8.4

Docker creates the volume automatically.

19. Docker Networks
List:

docker network ls

Create network:

docker network create mynetwork

Inspect:

docker network inspect mynetwork

Run container on network:

docker run -d \
  --name web \
  --network mynetwork \
  nginx

Another container:

docker run -d \
  --name app \
  --network mynetwork \
  nginx

Now containers can communicate using container names.

For example:

web
can be used as hostname.

20. Connect Existing Container to Network
docker network connect mynetwork mycontainer

Disconnect:

docker network disconnect mynetwork mycontainer

Remove network:

docker network rm mynetwork

21. Docker Hub
Login:

docker login

Tag image:

docker tag myapp username/myapp:v1

Push:

docker push username/myapp:v1

Pull:

docker pull username/myapp:v1

22. Docker Compose
Check Compose:

docker compose version

Create:

nano compose.yaml

Example:

services:

  web:
    image: nginx
    ports:
      - "8080:80"

  db:
    image: mysql:8.4
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root123
      MYSQL_DATABASE: testdb
      MYSQL_USER: user
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: user123

Start:

docker compose up -d

Check:

docker compose ps

Logs:

docker compose logs

Live logs:

docker compose logs -f

Stop:

docker compose stop

Start again:

docker compose start

Restart:

docker compose restart

Stop and remove containers/network:

docker compose down

Remove containers + volumes:

docker compose down -v

Build and start:

docker compose up -d --build

23. Three-Tier Docker Compose
This is very important for lab.

Architecture:

          USER
           |
           ↓
     ┌────────────┐
     │  FRONTEND  │
     │   NGINX    │
     └──────┬─────┘
            |
            ↓
     ┌────────────┐
     │  BACKEND   │
     │  PHP/API   │
     └──────┬─────┘
            |
            ↓
     ┌────────────┐
     │  DATABASE  │
     │   MYSQL    │
     └────────────┘
Example Compose:

services:

  frontend:
    image: nginx
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    networks:
      - app_network

  backend:
    image: php:8.3-apache
    networks:
      - app_network

  database:
    image: mysql:8.4
    environment:
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root123
      MYSQL_DATABASE: appdb
      MYSQL_USER: appuser
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: app123
    volumes:
      - db_data:/var/lib/mysql
    networks:
      - app_network

networks:
  app_network:

volumes:
  db_data:

Start:

docker compose up -d

Check:

docker compose ps

24. WordPress + MySQL Compose
Very common practical question.

services:

  db:
    image: mysql:8.4
    restart: unless-stopped
    environment:
      MYSQL_DATABASE: wordpress
      MYSQL_USER: wpuser
      MYSQL_PASSWORD: wp123
      MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root123
    volumes:
      - db_data:/var/lib/mysql

  wordpress:
    image: wordpress:latest
    restart: unless-stopped
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    environment:
      WORDPRESS_DB_HOST: db:3306
      WORDPRESS_DB_USER: wpuser
      WORDPRESS_DB_PASSWORD: wp123
      WORDPRESS_DB_NAME: wordpress
    depends_on:
      - db

volumes:
  db_data:

Run:

docker compose up -d

Check:

docker compose ps

Browser:

http://SERVER-IP:8080
25. Docker Compose YAML Important Parts
services
Defines containers.

services:

image
Which image to use.

image: nginx

ports
Host → Container.

ports:
  - "8080:80"

environment
Environment variables.

environment:
  MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: root123

volumes
Persistent storage.

volumes:
  - db_data:/var/lib/mysql

networks
Container communication.

networks:
  - app_network

depends_on
Startup dependency.

depends_on:
  - db

